From: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] phy: airoha: usb: only program the SerDes mux for the shared port

airoha_usb_phy_u3_set_mode() wrote SSTR.USB_PCIE_SEL unconditionally even
for the dedicated USB1 SerDes, stealing the shared USB2/PCIe2 SerDes away
from PCIe2 (6 GHz radio) whenever USB0 is enabled. Only program the mux
for AIROHA_SCU_SERDES_USB2.

Origin: archive/xr1710g-v1@e85677d284c0
Signed-off-by: genshanxinli <127909456+genshanxinli@users.noreply.github.com>
---
--- a/drivers/phy/airoha/phy-airoha-usb.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/airoha/phy-airoha-usb.c
@@ -418,10 +418,14 @@ static int airoha_usb_phy_u3_set_mode(st
 {
 	u32 sel;
 
-	/* Only USB2 supports PCIe mode */
-	if (mode == PHY_MODE_PCIE &&
-	    priv->serdes_port != AIROHA_SCU_SERDES_USB2)
-		return -EINVAL;
+	/* Only USB2 shares its SerDes mux (SSTR.USB_PCIE_SEL) with PCIe2;
+	 * USB1 has a dedicated USB-only SerDes and must not touch the mux.
+	 */
+	if (priv->serdes_port != AIROHA_SCU_SERDES_USB2) {
+		if (mode == PHY_MODE_PCIE)
+			return -EINVAL;
+		return 0;
+	}
 
 	if (mode == PHY_MODE_PCIE)
 		sel = AIROHA_SCU_SSTR_USB_PCIE_SEL_PCIE;
